  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 350°F. Line a large baking sheet pan with parchment paper. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse chickpeas, then pat dry with a clean towel or paper towels. Place in a medium bowl along with oil, sesame seeds, and spices, then stir to combine. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 (254 g) can garbanzo beans (chickpeas)\n2 tbsp extra virgin olive oil\n2 tsp sesame seeds\n1 tsp parsley flakes\n1 tsp garlic powder\n1 tsp onion powder\n¼ tsp salt\n½ tsp black pepper\n½ tsp smoked paprika"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer chickpeas to the baking sheet, spreading them out in a single layer (make sure the chickpeas are touching with no gaps). Evenly sprinkle cheese over top.",
      "secondary_message": "1 cup shredded cheese, Italian blend"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking sheet in the preheated oven and bake until chickpeas are golden brown and cheese is melted, about 20 minutes. Remove from oven and let cool, 5 minutes (the chickpeas will firm up as they cool). Leave the oven on.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer baked chickpeas to a cutting board, cut into \"chips\" using a knife, then return to the baking sheet. Place chips back in the oven and continue to bake until they are crisp, about 10 minutes. Remove from oven and transfer to a rack to cool, 10 minutes (they will firm up as they cool). \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer chickpea chips to a serving platter and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
